# 5. NON-NEGOTIABLE PRODUCT RULES

## Product positioning

Build a premium-feeling, accessible PDF productivity platform.

Primary homepage message:

**“A Better Way to Work with Documents.”**

The product should communicate simplicity, precision, reliability, privacy, productivity, professionalism, and accessibility.

Use a temporary brand name if the repository does not already contain a suitable product identity. Do not get stuck on naming.

## Completely free — no monetization

This is a strict product requirement.

Do not introduce:

- Pricing pages.
- Subscription plans.
- Free and Pro tiers.
- Premium features.
- Credit systems.
- Payment gateways.
- Paid downloads.
- Upgrade prompts.
- Usage-based paywalls.
- Account-based tool restrictions.
- Feature gating.
- Monetization-related banners or marketing.

Every implemented tool must be equally available to guests and registered users.

## Guest access is first-class

Users must be able to discover tools, upload documents, process documents, use the editor, and download results without creating an account.

Registration is optional.

Accounts may provide convenience features such as synchronized preferences, saved workspace configuration, optional document storage, and cross-device history.

An account must never unlock additional PDF tools or higher feature availability.

Guest and registered users must receive the same operational limits. Technical limits may depend on file size, page count, operation complexity, processing resources, or security considerations—but never on payment or account status.

## Absolutely no AI features

Do not include AI functionality of any kind.

No AI chat, assistant, summaries, translation, writing, document analysis, content generation, or question answering.

Conventional OCR, text extraction, metadata inspection, document comparison, and standard PDF processing are allowed.

